<title>GERMANY: German Bundesbank 1996 profit break-down.</title>
<headline>German Bundesbank 1996 profit break-down.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a break-down of the major components of the 1996 profits and balance sheet of Germany's central bank, the Bundesbank.</p>
<p>(billions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				   9.427   vs 10.928</p>
<p>    Transfer to Federal Government	 8.826   vs 10.318</p>
<p>    Interest received			  12.9    vs 15.1</p>
<p>    Expenses				     3.9     vs 4.7</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total			366.4   vs 354.4</p>
<p>Assets:</p>
<p>    External position			  121.0   vs 123.3</p>
<p>    Domestic lending			   226.2   vs 213.1</p>
<p>Liabilities:</p>
<p>    Banknotes in circulation		 260.4   vs 248.4</p>
<p>    Deposits				     53.6    vs 50.6</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
